-the one-in-N sampling rate is `max(1, ceil(V * 3000 / E / 4096))`, capped at uint32. It bootstraps
-at 1 before the first measured window. Each sampled visit adds its latched rate, so later rate
-changes cannot reinterpret old counters. Physical shard census moves with the shard; immutable
-bucket IDs carry controller history. The executor refreshes its cached rate only at the existing
